 "wall_clock_reduce_s": 34.5,
 "verdict_one_line": "FOR the paper's claim: at s_d = 0.01 the crossover load \u03b8* plateaus rather than drifting with lattice length (half-drop \u03b8* across L_long = 96: 0.70, 192: 0.58, 384: 0.52, 768: 0.60, 1536: 0.61; largest-minus-smallest-L difference -0.087 [-0.251, +0.083], no monotone trend; constant fit preferred over power-law+plateau, extrapolated large-L \u03b8* = 0.550 [0.530, 0.574]).",
 "against_paper": false,
 "censoring_treatment": "Right-censored runs (no fixation by the frame cap) enter the median estimators as the lower bound t_fix := numgen. This is exact for a median whenever fewer than half of an arm is censored. Only the 1536x32 neutral anchor arm has censored runs: 4 of 61 (cap 1e8 frames).",
 "deviations_executed_during_run": [
  {
